<title>GERMANY: German traders bid for free-mkt wheat at EU tender. [corrected 11:34 gmt]</title>
<headline>German traders bid for free-mkt wheat at EU tender. [corrected 11:34 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German traders bid for 22,000 (Corrects from 220,000) tonnes of free market soft wheat, at rebates of 15.98 to 19.78 Ecus a tonne, at this week's EU export tender, intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Bids were also made for 22,500 tonnes of barley at rebates of 26.94 to 30.25, BLE said.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom 49-228-26097150</p>
